T1.3  Security middleware
Date: 2026-11-21
Commands run:
  uv run pytest backend/tests/test_security.py -> 41 passed
  Manual (running server): Host: evil.example -> 403 forbidden_origin; POST with Origin https://evil.example -> 403
  Through the Vite proxy (T1.1 run 2 and the browser in T1.7): GET /api/health via 127.0.0.1:5173 -> 200,
    so the Host the proxy passes on (127.0.0.1:5173) is accepted (RK-3).
Cases: local Host on 8000/5173/8001/5174 accepted; foreign, portless, wrong-port, LAN and [::1] Hosts 403 (V-S01);
  POST/PATCH/DELETE with a foreign, API-port, "null" or missing Origin 403 and the endpoint never ran (V-S02);
  no access-control-* header on GET, POST or a preflight OPTIONS (V-S03); 2 MB body 413, streamed 1.5 MB body 413,
  just under 1 MB accepted, text/plain, form, multipart and missing Content-Type 415 (V-S06).
Decision within the spec: a changing request with no Origin header is refused (SEC-3: "isn't the app's own").
  Browsers always send Origin on POST/PATCH/DELETE, so the app is unaffected; other tools must send it.
Files changed: backend/app/security.py, backend/app/main.py (registration), backend/tests/test_security.py
Requirements covered: SEC-1 (servers bind 127.0.0.1), SEC-2, SEC-3, SEC-7 (size and type), ADR-002
Open issues: a good changing request through the proxy is first exercised end to end in Phase 3, when a write
  endpoint exists. The unknown-field 422 of V-S06 is checked on the schemas (T1.6), and through the API in
  Phase 2. V-S10 (socket check) is T4.1.

