T1.6  API contract (schemas)
Date: 2026-11-21
Commands run:
  uv run pytest backend/tests/test_organizations.py test_deals.py test_contacts.py test_activities.py -> 107 passed
Contract: request models (extra="forbid") OrganizationCreate/Update, ContactCreate/Update, DealCreate/Update,
  DealMove, ActivityCreate/Update; response models Organization, Contact, Deal, MoveResult, Activity, Source,
  TimelineEntry, Organization/Contact/DealDeleteImpact, Dashboard (Summary, WonThisMonth, WinRate, MonthFigures,
  FunnelStage, OpenStage, FollowUp, FollowUps, DashboardCounts), Health. Field names and order are checked
  against spec 5.3 in the tests, and spec 5.5's example validates and round-trips.
R21 validators: trimming and blank = empty, names 1-200, email shape and 254, phone characters and 40, website
  http/https kept, bare domain prefixed, other schemes (javascript:, data:, mailto:, ftp:) refused, 2,048 after
  the prefix, industry and job title 100, notes and description 5,000, value 0-1e9 and probability 0-100 as
  whole numbers (no floats, strings or booleans), real YYYY-MM-DD dates, local date-times with no time zone,
  positive IDs, exactly one activity parent, PATCH can't null a required field (R34: links left out aren't
  checked), unknown fields 422 "This field isn't allowed.".
Files changed: backend/app/schemas.py, backend/app/errors.py (field messages), backend/tests/test_organizations.py,
  test_deals.py, test_contacts.py, test_activities.py
Requirements covered: R10-R13, R21, spec 5.1-5.5 shapes, SEC-6 (scheme check), SEC-7 (unknown fields)
Open issues (sent to the engineer for confirmation before the contract freezes at C1):
  - spec 5.5 doesn't give item shapes for follow_ups.* and recent. Implemented: a follow-up is the Activity
    shape plus `source` {kind, id, name}; a recent item is the TimelineEntry shape.
  - Delete impact: one model per resource with only the keys that apply (organization: contacts_kept,
    deals_kept; contact: deals_kept, activities_deleted; deal: activities_deleted, stage_changes_deleted), as
    spec 5.3's rule says, rather than its four-key example.

